@lu Ech mengen, et ass net typesch, mee ech hunn de Wanter gär.
@distractor-lu Summer
@distractor-lu Reen
@en I think it is not typical, but I like the winter.
@distractor-en summer
@distractor-en rain

@sentence
@question Firwat hutt Dir de Wanter gär?
@lu Ech hunn de Schnéi richteg gär, an am Wanter ass Chrëschtdag.
@distractor-lu Reen
@distractor-lu Hierscht
@en I really like the snow, and in the winter there is Christmas Day.
@distractor-en rain
@distractor-en autumn

@sentence
@question Wat ass Är Liblingsjoreszäit, wann Dir un d'Wieder denkt?
@lu Dat ass eng schwiereg Fro: mäi Gebuertsdag ass am Summer, mee d'Wieder hunn ech am léifste am Wanter.
@distractor-lu einfach
@distractor-lu Hierscht
@en That is a demanding question: my birthday is in the summer, but the weather I like best in the winter.
@distractor-en easy
@distractor-en autumn

@sentence
@question Wéi ee Wanter mengt Dir?
@lu Ech mengen net de lëtzebuergesche Wanter, mee de Wanter an de Bierger mat Schnéi a Sonn.
@distractor-lu Reen
@distractor-lu Strand
@en I do not mean the Luxembourgish winter, but the winter in the mountains with snow and sun.
@distractor-en rain
@distractor-en beach

@sentence
@question Wéi eng Joreszäit hutt Dir am mannste gär?
@lu Ech hunn et net gär, wann et wierklech dreckeg ass, an dat ass oft am Fréijoer an am spéiden Hierscht.
@distractor-lu propper
@distractor-lu Summer
@en I do not like it when it is really dirty, and that is often in the spring and in the late autumn.
@distractor-en clean
@distractor-en summer

@sentence
@question Wat mengt Dir mat "dreckeg"?
@lu Dann ass et schwéier fir an de Bësch ze goen, well am Bësch naass an dreckeg ass.
@distractor-lu einfach
@distractor-lu Stad
@en Then it is difficult to go into the forest, because in the forest it is wet and dirty.
@distractor-en easy
@distractor-en city

